WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:14.239
Mr. Ribbit, the science teacher, cleared his throat.

2
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:20.083
"Ribbit! Do you know how we became frogs?" he croaked.

3
00:00:20.084 --> 00:00:27.235
The young frogs looked at each other.

4
00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:30.238
Mr. Ribbit held up two pictures.

5
00:00:30.239 --> 00:00:33.800
In one hand was a picture of a tadpole.

6
00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:36.813
In the other was a picture of a frog.

7
00:00:36.814 --> 00:00:43.449
"Today we are going to learn about metamorphosis. Ribbit!" he said.

8
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.604
"Meta . . . what?" asked Freddy.

9
00:00:46.605 --> 00:00:50.144
"Metamorphosis," Mr. Ribbit repeated.

10
00:00:50.145 --> 00:00:55.479
"It is how we change from tadpoles into frogs.

11
00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:00.892
In the spring male frogs attract female frogs by singing.

12
00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:05.374
The frog couple starts their family in the pond. Ribbit!

13
00:01:05.375 --> 00:01:09.400
The male frog fertilizes the eggs in the water.

14
00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:13.509
A few days later, the eggs begin to change."

15
00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.900
"Do they become tadpoles?" asked Hetty.

16
00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:27.480
"Ribbit! Yes. At this stage, the head is big and the tail is very long," explained Mr. Ribbit.

17
00:01:27.481 --> 00:01:31.863
"Soon the eggs hatch and the tadpoles come out.

18
00:01:31.864 --> 00:01:36.215
Tadpoles, like fish, use gills to breathe."

19
00:01:36.216 --> 00:01:43.914
"But Mr. Ribbit, we aren't fish, are we?" asked Lily.

20
00:01:43.915 --> 00:01:48.349
"Of course not! We are amphibians.

21
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.200
Who knows what that means?"

22
00:01:51.201 --> 00:01:56.367
"Amphibians can live on land and in water," answered Boris.

23
00:01:56.368 --> 00:02:04.167
"Right! But at first, tadpoles can only live in the water."

24
00:02:04.168 --> 00:02:07.454
"What do tadpoles eat?" asked Freddy.

25
00:02:07.455 --> 00:02:13.838
"Ribbit! As soon as they are born, tadpoles eat plants and algae.

26
00:02:13.839 --> 00:02:17.514
A few days later, they develop teeth.

27
00:02:17.515 --> 00:02:24.150
Then the tadpoles start to eat insects."

28
00:02:24.151 --> 00:02:29.056
Mr. Ribbit continued, "Tadpoles use their tails to swim.

29
00:02:29.057 --> 00:02:32.231
They are very active at this age.

30
00:02:32.232 --> 00:02:38.259
Tadpoles swim around in a group called a school.

31
00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:45.124
Six to nine weeks after they are born, metamorphosis begins. Ribbit!

32
00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:50.976
The back legs begin to appear and the tadpoles use them for swimming.

33
00:02:50.977 --> 00:02:55.850
The body grows larger, and the head begins to take shape.

34
00:02:55.851 --> 00:03:00.110
Next, the front legs begin to grow."

35
00:03:00.111 --> 00:03:05.821
"That looks like my brother!" Hetty laughed.

36
00:03:05.822 --> 00:03:12.554
"Ribbit! It looks just like a small frog except for the long tail.

37
00:03:12.555 --> 00:03:18.060
The tadpole is almost a frog now," said Mr. Ribbit.

38
00:03:18.061 --> 00:03:24.716
"During the last days of metamorphosis, the tail slowly disappears into the body.

39
00:03:24.717 --> 00:03:28.250
Remember the tadpoles' gills? Ribbit!

40
00:03:28.251 --> 00:03:30.596
They don't need them any more.

41
00:03:30.597 --> 00:03:33.945
The gills are covered over by skin.

42
00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:39.893
So the little frogs learn to breathe with their lungs.

43
00:03:39.894 --> 00:03:44.994
Once the tail is gone, the little ones can climb onto land.

44
00:03:44.995 --> 00:03:54.122
Now the tadpole is completely transformed into a frog.

45
00:03:54.123 --> 00:03:58.504
In a few days, the new frogs can leave the pond.

46
00:03:58.505 --> 00:04:03.663
They can enjoy life both in the pond and on land.

47
00:04:03.664 --> 00:04:08.722
Metamorphosis takes about 12 to 16 weeks.

48
00:04:08.723 --> 00:04:11.830
There are many different kinds of frogs.

49
00:04:11.831 --> 00:04:14.280
Some like to live in the water.

50
00:04:14.281 --> 00:04:17.480
Others spend all their time on the land.

51
00:04:17.481 --> 00:04:26.688
But we always have to return to the water to start our own families," concluded Mr. Ribbit.

52
00:04:26.689 --> 00:04:33.699
"Wow! We are special in many ways!" Victor exclaimed.

53
00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:38.909
"It's interesting to know how we got here," the young frogs croaked.

54
00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:46.133
"We are proud to be frogs! Ribbit!"
